      "worked_solution": "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\nV=702,\\,l=13,\\,w=6\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}702 & =13\\cdot 6\\cdot h \\\\ 702 & =78h \\\\ h & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the height is $9\\,\\text{m}.$",
